# Minor fix #6: this used to be a denylist (exclude src/**, test/**,
# **/*.ts, dist/*.js, ...) built on the assumption that the esbuild bundle
# is named dist/extension.cjs. That assumption is invisible here — nothing
# enforces it — so changing esbuild's `--outfile` extension to `.js` (e.g.
# to match this package's own `"type": "module"`) would make the bundle
# ALSO match the `dist/*.js` exclusion meant only for tsc's per-module
# output, and the .vsix would silently ship an empty `dist/`: a dead
# extension that installs cleanly and does nothing (exactly the "green
# tests, clean types, dead artifact" failure mode Finding I5 is about).
#
# An allowlist confines that coupling to ONE line that names the bundle
# explicitly, instead of a denylist rule (`dist/*.js`) whose stated purpose
# — excluding tsc's per-module output — has nothing to do with the bundle's
# name, so nobody renaming `--outfile` would think to look here. A future
# rename still needs this line updated too (no static ignore-file can
# detect its own staleness), but `npm run package`'s own "Files included in
# the VSIX" listing now makes an empty `dist/` immediately visible if it
# isn't — and CI's own bundle-verification step (Finding I5) reads
# dist/extension.cjs directly and fails loudly, rather than silently, if
# that exact file is missing.
**
!package.json
!dist/extension.cjs
